# ESP-IDF build output
/build/
sdkconfig
sdkconfig.old
managed_components/
dependencies.lock

# Staged release BINARIES belong on the GitHub release, not in git - but the
# notes and publish script are source and should be versioned.
/dist/**
!/dist/**/
!/dist/**/*.md
!/dist/**/*.sh

# host test binaries
*.exe
*.o
*.obj

# editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Vendor firmware and captures: NEVER commit HarvestRight's code ---
#
# A flash dump of the official adapter, or a decoded dryer image, is their
# copyrighted binary. Our own analysis and notes belong in the repo; their bytes
# do not. This repo is pushed to GitHub, and `git add -A` is one keystroke, so
# the safeguard lives here rather than in anyone's memory.
*.bin
*.srec
*.h6r
*.b6r
*.hfs
*.hft

# Adapter interrogation transcripts: our own observations, but they carry the
# machine's serial number and UID. Force-add deliberately if a capture is worth
# sharing, after checking what is in it.
adapter-transcript-*.txt

# Dryer-simulator transcripts: same class. They log the UID frame, which
# carries the machine unique ID HarvestRight binds to an account, plus the
# user-set machine name. Nine of these accumulated in one afternoon and a
# single `git add -A` would have published them.
dryer-sim-*.txt
screen-map-*.txt

# Backup of the stock adapter's USB volume: vendor firmware plus device
# identifiers (MAC). Analysis notes are fine in the repo; this is not.
/drive backup/
